WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.356
- Good morning believe nation,

00:00:01.356 --> 00:00:04.942
today's message is, "Do one thing."

00:00:04.942 --> 00:00:07.028
Over to you Robert Rodriguez.

00:00:07.028 --> 00:00:09.025
(rooster crowing)

00:00:09.025 --> 00:00:11.661
♫ I wake up every morning

00:00:11.661 --> 00:00:14.585
♫ Espresso keep me going

00:00:14.585 --> 00:00:18.829
♫ I wake up every morning ♫

00:00:18.829 --> 00:00:20.344
- There's this book called, The One Thing,

00:00:20.344 --> 00:00:21.203
have you ever seen that?

00:00:21.203 --> 00:00:22.230
It says you should just do one thing.

00:00:22.230 --> 00:00:23.908
And I go, "Well, I shouldn't
even bother reading that.

00:00:23.908 --> 00:00:24.883
"That doesn't apply to me."

00:00:24.883 --> 00:00:26.108
But then I thought about it.

00:00:26.108 --> 00:00:27.536
It's like, "Well I do one thing,

00:00:27.536 --> 00:00:29.458
"I live a creative life."

00:00:29.458 --> 00:00:32.395
Everything you do you
apply a creativity to it.

00:00:32.395 --> 00:00:33.904
Whether it's the way
you meet with a friend

00:00:33.904 --> 00:00:36.958
and you make them dinner or
you do stuff with your kids.

00:00:36.958 --> 00:00:39.135
And then when you go, and
you're working on an idea

00:00:39.135 --> 00:00:40.568
and you're doing music as the same time

00:00:40.568 --> 00:00:41.712
while you're on the set.

00:00:41.712 --> 00:00:43.268
You're never in a block because

00:00:43.268 --> 00:00:44.655
you're always actually in a flow.

00:00:44.655 --> 00:00:47.099
If you don't live your life creatively

00:00:47.099 --> 00:00:49.467
and then you set aside some time at night

00:00:49.467 --> 00:00:50.611
to go write your novel,

00:00:50.611 --> 00:00:52.939
you're going to get a block
because you're not in the flow.

00:00:52.939 --> 00:00:55.760
But if you apply creativity
to everything in your life,

00:00:55.760 --> 00:00:57.769
everything is available to you.

00:00:57.769 --> 00:00:59.481
To where suddenly you can paint.

00:00:59.481 --> 00:01:01.484
You'll see paintings
I did with the actors.

00:01:01.484 --> 00:01:03.237
Even though they are very
creative in the acting world,

00:01:03.237 --> 00:01:04.502
they didn't think they could paint.

00:01:04.502 --> 00:01:06.737
So I made them paint and then
they saw they were able to

00:01:06.737 --> 00:01:08.252
because when you are in a creative flow

00:01:08.252 --> 00:01:10.290
you can do just about anything.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:12.774
So it's all about living a creative life

00:01:12.774 --> 00:01:15.839
to where you can't
possibly ever get blocked

00:01:15.839 --> 00:01:17.807
because you're always,

00:01:17.807 --> 00:01:19.439
"Okay, I have an idea for writing

00:01:19.439 --> 00:01:20.623
"so I'm going to go cook something"

00:01:20.623 --> 00:01:21.929
Which is art you can eat.

00:01:21.929 --> 00:01:23.723
You know, and you're serving
it and you're eating it,

00:01:23.723 --> 00:01:24.820
and consuming it and you're creating.

00:01:24.820 --> 00:01:25.923
And you go back and you do that.

00:01:25.923 --> 00:01:26.756
Does that make sense?

00:01:26.756 --> 00:01:28.489
- Yeah, there's no
structured boxes around it.

00:01:28.489 --> 00:01:29.888
It's like a lifestyle.

00:01:29.888 --> 00:01:32.453
- There's no delineation
between work and play.

00:01:32.453 --> 00:01:33.440
It's all play.

00:01:33.440 --> 00:01:35.559
- This is why it's so important
to find your one word.

00:01:35.559 --> 00:01:39.448
Because it's not just about
doing one thing, one task,

00:01:39.448 --> 00:01:41.898
it's about living one way.

00:01:41.898 --> 00:01:45.409
Your way, on purpose and
knowing what that is.

00:01:45.409 --> 00:01:47.568
So if I look at this clip as an example,

00:01:47.568 --> 00:01:50.349
Robert's one word is
likely creative, right?

00:01:50.349 --> 00:01:51.498
He wants to be creative.

00:01:51.498 --> 00:01:53.292
He wants to live in a creative way.

00:01:53.292 --> 00:01:56.276
It's not just doing one task all day long,

00:01:56.276 --> 00:01:59.138
but doing creative work all day long.

00:01:59.138 --> 00:02:00.815
That's where he comes alive.

00:02:00.815 --> 00:02:02.975
And if you try to put Robert in a room

00:02:02.975 --> 00:02:05.349
with no doors and no windows,

00:02:05.349 --> 00:02:07.108
and just lock him in there in a cell

00:02:07.108 --> 00:02:09.633
and told him what to do, he would die.

00:02:09.633 --> 00:02:12.698
If you starved all the
creativity out of him

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:15.757
and forced him to do
something he would hate it.

00:02:15.757 --> 00:02:16.657
He would struggle,

00:02:16.657 --> 00:02:18.335
nobody would know who he was.

00:02:18.335 --> 00:02:19.966
And that's most people.

00:02:19.966 --> 00:02:22.166
Most people have no idea who they are,

00:02:22.166 --> 00:02:23.999
and are stuck in a box

00:02:25.359 --> 00:02:27.483
that somebody else has made for them,

00:02:27.483 --> 00:02:28.987
and they don't know how to get out.

00:02:28.987 --> 00:02:30.374
They don't know what their one word is.

00:02:30.374 --> 00:02:31.843
They don't know how to break free.

00:02:31.843 --> 00:02:34.245
They don't know how to
design a life on purpose.

00:02:34.245 --> 00:02:36.492
It's why it's so important to understand

00:02:36.492 --> 00:02:39.057
what the one word is for you,

00:02:39.057 --> 00:02:43.057
that now you can create
something and design it.

00:02:43.057 --> 00:02:45.750
A life and a business
around what you want to do.

00:02:45.750 --> 00:02:47.103
So lets look at creativity,

00:02:47.103 --> 00:02:48.821
let's look at Robert a little bit more.

00:02:48.821 --> 00:02:52.043
All the people that he
surrounds himself with

00:02:52.043 --> 00:02:55.236
should be people who help
him be more creative.

00:02:55.236 --> 00:02:59.003
All the content that he
consumes on a daily basis,

00:02:59.003 --> 00:03:00.275
I don't know what his habits are.

00:03:00.275 --> 00:03:01.209
Is he reading books?

00:03:01.209 --> 00:03:02.515
Is he watching YouTube videos?

00:03:02.515 --> 00:03:03.624
Is he checking out the news?

00:03:03.624 --> 00:03:04.942
Is he going to theaters?

00:03:04.942 --> 00:03:06.207
Is he going to the movies?

00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:08.953
The content that he consumes

00:03:08.953 --> 00:03:12.587
should make him feel more creative.

00:03:12.587 --> 00:03:14.671
His daily habits and rituals,

00:03:14.671 --> 00:03:16.517
whatever that looks like,

00:03:16.517 --> 00:03:18.514
whether it's meditation,

00:03:18.514 --> 00:03:22.554
or doing yoga, or watching
some YouTube videos,

00:03:22.554 --> 00:03:24.645
watching Entspresso in the morning,

00:03:24.645 --> 00:03:26.155
those things should be designed

00:03:26.155 --> 00:03:28.071
to help him be more creative.

00:03:28.071 --> 00:03:31.171
And so once you understand
what the one word is for you,

00:03:31.171 --> 00:03:33.133
what the one way is for you,

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:34.613
when you figure that out,

00:03:34.613 --> 00:03:36.691
then you look at your life.

00:03:36.691 --> 00:03:40.900
You look at what your typical
weekly schedule looks like.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:42.822
You look at the things
that you are consuming

00:03:42.822 --> 00:03:43.849
on a daily basis.

00:03:43.849 --> 00:03:44.682
You look at the people that

00:03:44.682 --> 00:03:47.343
you're hanging around with constantly.

00:03:47.343 --> 00:03:51.336
And how many of those people,
activities and things,

00:03:51.336 --> 00:03:55.503
help that one way, help that
one word come out of you.

00:03:56.463 --> 00:03:58.211
And for a lot of people at the start

00:03:58.211 --> 00:04:00.910
it's a really sobering experience.

00:04:00.910 --> 00:04:02.008
For a lot of people,

00:04:02.008 --> 00:04:03.360
like if you're unhappy with your life,

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.409
if you feel like you have a huge ceiling

00:04:05.409 --> 00:04:08.811
and you're not anywhere close
to reaching your potential

00:04:08.811 --> 00:04:11.139
it's because a lot of the
people, things, and habits

00:04:11.139 --> 00:04:14.689
that you have on a daily
basis are not coming out.

00:04:14.689 --> 00:04:17.023
They're suppressing you.

00:04:17.023 --> 00:04:19.194
They're keeping you in your box,

00:04:19.194 --> 00:04:21.411
and it starts because you don't
even have the self awareness

00:04:21.411 --> 00:04:23.455
to know what your one word is.

00:04:23.455 --> 00:04:25.254
You don't have the self awareness to know

00:04:25.254 --> 00:04:27.710
what the one thing is
that you should be doing.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:30.618
What the one way of living
is and you should be living.

00:04:30.618 --> 00:04:32.174
So figure it out.

00:04:32.174 --> 00:04:34.676
Then do an audit of your life,

00:04:34.676 --> 00:04:37.207
and the habits, and the
things that are around you.

00:04:37.207 --> 00:04:40.075
Say, "Does this help me believe more,

00:04:40.075 --> 00:04:43.273
or create more, or care more?"

00:04:43.273 --> 00:04:44.606
It's the unlock.

00:04:45.938 --> 00:04:47.168
It gives you certainty.

00:04:47.168 --> 00:04:48.277
It give you clarity.

00:04:48.277 --> 00:04:49.258
It gives you power,

00:04:49.258 --> 00:04:51.592
and it lets you do amazing things.

00:04:51.592 --> 00:04:53.031
So the question to think today is,

00:04:53.031 --> 00:04:56.149
I'm curious what is the one
way that you want to live.

00:04:56.149 --> 00:04:58.831
What is the one word core value for you,

00:04:58.831 --> 00:05:01.336
and once you figure that out,

00:05:01.336 --> 00:05:05.358
what's one thing that you
need to start changing.

00:05:05.358 --> 00:05:07.616
What's the one thing in your
life that does not support you

00:05:07.616 --> 00:05:11.134
being creative, or
believing, or caring more,

00:05:11.134 --> 00:05:13.015
and you need to eliminate
that from your life.

00:05:13.015 --> 00:05:14.170
Super curious to find out.

00:05:14.170 --> 00:05:15.563
Leave it down in the comments below,

00:05:15.563 --> 00:05:17.078
and we'll join in discussion.

